 "honest_headline_sentence": "Under equal weight per benchmark cell (8 cells, 1/8 each), the accuracy-max setting beats always-32B-direct on accuracy by +0.0007 [-0.0025, +0.0036] -- but it now costs 1.83x that baseline's compute, not less, and the compute-lean setting neither matches it on the multiple-choice half (-0.0070 [-0.0126, -0.0017], a SIGNIFICANT LOSS) nor stays cheap (1.59x compute, up from 0.51x sample-weighted); the one baseline the method still clearly beats at equal weight is a 32B actually made to reason (+0.0599 [+0.0498, +0.0697] accuracy, -88% latency, -83% energy -- though not fewer FLOP-eq: 1.83x as charged, 1.47x honestly re-costed)."
